  "gaps": [
    "The student's chosen concentration is not known; the 18-credit concentration block is recorded as a single requirement. Options listed: Artificial Intelligence in Criminal Justice (online only), Digital Forensics and Cybersecurity, Crime and Criminal Behavior, Criminal Justice Administration, National Security, Emergency Response and Crisis Leadership, and Probation and Parole.",
    "The Crime and Criminal Behavior and Criminal Justice Administration concentrations each list a 'CRJ 310 or CRJ 400' choice and also list CRJ 400 separately. The capture does not explain how these overlap.",
    "Catalog year/term is not stated in the capture.",
    "Minimum grade requirements and general degree conferral rules are referenced (Undergraduate Degree Conferral Requirements) but not included in the capture.",
    "The capture does not state any residency or institutional-credit requirement (courses that must be completed at Strayer).",
    "Transfer credit limits and policies are not stated in the capture.",
    "Rules for the elective component (e.g., minor options, level restrictions) are not specified beyond consultation with a dean, advisor or coach."
